course: dictionary
lesson: 7034
title: Particularly and not particularly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Particularly means especially, or more than usual or more than others. «I particularly like apples» means apples are your favourite out of all the fruit you could pick. The word tells you that one thing stands out from the rest.
explain: Look at the words around it to check. «It was particularly cold that night» tells you the night was colder than an ordinary night. Try swapping in especially: «It was especially cold that night» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «Not particularly» means not very or not really. If someone asks, «Are you hungry?» and you reply, «Not particularly», you are saying only a little, not much. It is a polite, soft way to answer, so it does not sound too blunt.
fact: Particularly means especially, or more than usual or more than others.
fact: «Particularly» can pick out one thing from a group, as in «particularly good».
fact: «Not particularly» means not very, or not really.
fact: Old-fashioned: «particularly» can also mean in detail or carefully, as in «she looked at it particularly».
fact: Particularly is an adverb, so it tells you more about another word, such as the adjective cold in «particularly cold».
exercise: «I particularly like apples.» What does particularly mean here? | Quickly | *Especially, more than the other fruit | Only sometimes, when I remember | Not at all
exercise: «Are you hungry?» «Not particularly.» What does the answer mean? | *Not very, or not really | Yes, very hungry | Dinner is ready | Please pass the bread
exercise: In «It was particularly cold that night», which word does particularly describe? | night | *cold | It | was
test: «The plant grew particularly well in sunlight.» What does particularly well suggest? | Badly and slowly | *Especially well, better than usual | Well, but only in the dark | Not at all
test: Which phrase means not very? | *not particularly | particularly if | particularly good | particularly when
exam: «You're very alike in many respects — particularly about the figure.» What does particularly show in this sentence? | *The figure is the point that stands out most | The respects are not important | Alike means different | The respects are all the same
